WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.290
This year, we saw no shortage of experimental
indie projects and blockbusters that defied

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.960
convention to shock audiences.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.040
Want to watch a film that has you wide-eyed
and open-mouthed by the time the credits start

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:11.540
to roll?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.620
Check out a few of the most baffling movies
of 2018.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.040
Suspiria may be a remake, but this modern
take on Dario Argento's 1977 film stands apart

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.160
from other 2018 horror films.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.760
When Susie, played by Dakota Johnson, is admitted
to a dance academy in West Berlin, the Academy

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.040
is still reeling over the disappearance of
a student.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.260
Before her disappearance, the student confessed
that she believed the academy was run by a

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.620
coven of witches, and as it turns out, she
might not have been crazy after all.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.200
Suspiria is a disturbing body horror packed
with trippy imagery.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.400
It's like watching a feature shot in hall
of mirrors.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.940
Told in six distinct narrative acts, the film
makes it difficult to distinguish what's real

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.860
and what's merely a product of the characters'
imaginations.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.840
Starring Lakeith Stanfield as Cassius Green
and Tessa Thompson as his artistic girlfriend

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.539
Detroit, Sorry to Bother You begins as a film
about a desperate telemarketer trying to pay

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:15.420
his rent, but turns into an absurdist dark
comedy that subverts all expectations by the

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:15.920
third act.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.920
As his coworkers unionize to protest their
low pay, Cassius tells himself that he can

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:25.289
support them from the other side of the picket
line, but he gets swept up into a conspiracy

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:26.540
that he never saw coming.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.060
Sorry to Bother You is easily one of the strangest
and best movies in decades.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:36.920
Starring Nicolas Cage as Red and Andrea Riseborough
as his titular companion, Mandy is easily

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.220
some of Cage's best work in recent years.

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:44.259
The plot follows Red and Mandy as they live
a happy, reclusive life... until Mandy is

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.380
kidnapped by a violent hippie cult.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:51.500
Directed by Panos Cosmatos', Mandy delves
into gory, psychedelic imagery that you can't

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.240
look away from.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:57.120
As the film progresses, the line between fantasy
and reality is so heavily blurred that you're

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.680
left unsure of what to believe.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.499
Assassination Nation quickly builds into something
much more sinister and terrifying than you

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.780
could have ever expected.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:09.480
When a hacker starts revealing the personal
messages of a small town, the airing of dirty

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.980
laundry turns from petty high school drama
into a full-blown bloody conflict.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.840
Assassination Nation takes a predictable premise
and jacks it all the way up to the most extreme

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.080
possible conclusion.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.100
As more secrets are revealed, the degradation
of social norms occurs so quickly that it's

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:29.439
safe to assume it wouldn't be a realistic
turn of events in real life, but it's worth

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.440
asking, "what if?"

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.320
In First Reformed, Reverend Ernst Toller holds
services at a church with a dwindling congregation.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.200
As he's grappling with the death of his son,
Toller gets a frantic call from one of his

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:40.700
flock.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:45.360
She's worried about her husband Michael, a
radical environmentalist who sees no hope

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:45.860
for the planet.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.530
As Toller attempts to counsel Mary and Michael,
he's forced to think about his own beliefs

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.000
and worry about the current state of the human
race.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.960
Directed by Paul Schrader, and starring Ethan
Hawke as Reverend Toller and Amanda Seyfried

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.920
as Mary, First Reformed refuses to wrap up
neatly for the viewer.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.159
After watching First Reformed, you can't help
but wonder if the doomsday believers have

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.300
a point after all.

00:03:07.689 --> 00:03:14.920
"Every tiny insect, the whole world is a manifestation
of his holy presence, I think this is an issue

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.660
where the church can lead!"

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.159
Annihilation is one of those genre-bending
films that combines the best of science fiction

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.640
and horror into a single compelling storyline.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:29.620
Kane, played by Oscar Isaac, is the only survivor
of an expedition into "The Shimmer," an electromagnetic

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.640
field that's spreading on the southern coast
of the United States.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.060
What really happened while he was inside,
and was it really Kane who came back?

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.840
A scientist, played by Natalie Portman, is
determined to find out with her own expedition.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.100
As she ventures into the Shimmer herself,
nothing is quite what it seems.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.800
"It's in me."

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.140
"It'll be in all of us."

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.840
The Happytime Murders follows a human and
puppet detective team as they try to figure

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.200
out who's behind the recent murders of retired
sitcom stars.

00:04:02.529 --> 00:04:07.140
With puppets engaging in everything from violent
crime to petty theft and raunchy jokes, it's

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.640
like a twisted look at your childhood favorites.

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:13.360
You won't be able to look at a puppet quite
the same way after watching The Happytime

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:13.960
Murders.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.560
Sure, you've got to give the cast and crew
props for their willingness to get creative

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.019
in the medium, but it's hard not to wonder
why this story had to be told with puppets,

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.360
which is truly baffling.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:28.620
In Madeline's Madeline, Helena Howard stars
as Madeline, a young woman who joins a prestigious

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.860
"physical theater" troupe.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:35.060
Her intensely ambitious director pushes her
to explore her family trauma through her art,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.960
particularly her relationship with her mother.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:42.660
But Madeline's performance begins to cross
from art into life, until the two become completely

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.360
indistinguishable.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.120
At its core, Madeline's Madeline is a film
about acting.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:52.300
It represents a look inside the mind of an
artist, complete with dizzying, dramatic cinematography.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.300
The characters explore identity through performance,
and the movie encourages viewers to consider

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.699
how much of our own identities are authentic
parts of who we are, and how much is merely

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.120
a performance for others.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.780
"Okay.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.340
Excuse me.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.300
Hi, yeah.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.200
Okay.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.000
Right."

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.300
In the suspenseful thriller Unsane, Claire
Foy plays Sawyer, a woman who moves away from

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.700
home to escape her stalker.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:21.180
But even after she thinks she's in the clear,
Sawyer struggles to move on and meets with

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.540
a counselor to dig into the healing process.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:28.420
Unfortunately, she ends up being tricked into
a long-term stay in a psychiatric institution,

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.820
where she makes a terrifying discovery.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.980
Watching Unsane will have you questioning
everyone around you for days after.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.360
"Your name is Sawyer Valentini."

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.660
"You know that already."

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.660
"By signing this, you've consented to voluntary
commitment for 24 hours."

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:44.800
"...No."

